# Store every text file with LF in the repository, whatever the checkout does.
#
# Added before the first real commit deliberately: without it, committing from
# Windows records CRLF for some files and LF for others depending on who touched
# them last, and a later fix rewrites thousands of lines in a diff that hides the
# actual change. `text=auto` lets Git detect text vs binary, so the JPEGs under
# assets/ and public/ are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Lockfiles are generated — never worth a merge conflict resolution by hand.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated

# Drizzle writes these; they are data, not code to review line by line.
drizzle/meta/*.json -diff linguist-generated
